  "term": "pulvinar",
  "definition": "The pulvinar is a large group of nerve cell clusters that makes up the most rear part of the thalamus. It lies above the geniculate bodies and the upper side of the midbrain, and it is divided into lateral, medial, inferior, and oral parts.",
